d2full 0016: a game's player starts with no items' or Battle Orders' shares on its maxima. World::enter reuses the last game's Player, so after Save and Exit and a new game in the same session the first stats refresh took the old shares off the save's own maxima, and the next save went under 0 and wrapped in its 21 bits (45 max life saved as 4141). One concern: save maxima.

--- a/components/game/world.cpp
+++ b/components/game/world.cpp
@@ -977,6 +977,11 @@
         actor->character.character_class = entering.character_class; actor->character.name = entering.name;
         actor->character.appearance = entering.appearance; actor->character.items = entering.items; actor->character.stats = entering.stats; actor->character.panel = entering.panel;
         actor->character.expansion = entering.expansion; actor->character.header = entering.header; actor->character.merc_items = entering.merc_items;
+        // d2full: the save's maxima are its own (Fight::own_stats takes the items' and Battle Orders' shares off), and
+        // Player stays from the last game: without this the next refresh took the old shares off the new maxima,
+        // and the save went under 0 and wrapped (21 bits: 45 max life saved as 4141 after Save and Exit, re-enter).
+        actor->item_max = {};
+        actor->bo_life = actor->bo_mana = 0;
         // A new game starts at full life, mana and stamina, whatever the
         // save held (D2's "save and exit to heal").
         static constexpr std::pair<d2d::d2s::StatId, d2d::d2s::StatId> kRefill[] = {
